OL,3,GNEWSAWhy do the White House Farm
OL,4,Amurders still grip people 40 years on?
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe murders of five people at an Essex
OL,7,Ffarmhouse was an unspeakable act of
OL,8,Fviolence. Six-year-old twins, a model
OL,9,Fand her adoptive parents dead ` it set
OL,10,Fthe stage for the ultimate whodunnit.
OL,11,FForty years on from Jeremy Bamber's
OL,12,Fconviction, why do the White House Farm
OL,13,Fmurders remain so compelling?
OL,15,FBamber killed his adoptive parents,
OL,16,Fsister and her twin sons on a summer's
OL,17,Fnight at their remote Georgian
OL,18,Ffarmhouse in Tolleshunt D'Arcy, Essex.
OL,20,FA year later, after a trial that
OL,21,Fgripped the nation, he was convicted of
OL,22,Ftheir murders on 28 October 1986.
OL,23,APub: 24-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
